From 538767a61c44898d2364fdb6b2a02fee813a8e54 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:55:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): phantom-ref checks consult this host's Board
 replica before calling an id phantom [daveey]

worker-1 completing t_01a1ceb5fa5abe36 (run 13081): the completion gate refused created_cards
t_01a1cedb2faf7341 (created on worker-3 by an earlier run of the same card, linked as its child), and
the summary scan flagged t_01a1cf4d49ca68bb (created on the hub 2 min earlier). Both cards were in
worker-1's Board replica (kanban/sync-shadow/default.db, 9.7k cards); its live kanban.db holds 227.

Why the earlier fix 0b1715a3f43 didn't hold: it only made "no hub replica" non-authoritative on a
Board-synced host. Here a fresh hub replica answered authoritatively without the 2-minute-old card,
and the created_cards gate never consulted any replica at all (live file only).

Now both the created_cards gate (_verify_created_cards) and the summary scan / prose_phantom_refs
diagnostic first look ids up in every sync-shadow/<board>.db, read-only (never creating a file;
an unreadable replica is skipped). The gate keeps its trust rule: a replica card counts only if its
created_by is the completer's assignee/id or the replica links it as the completer's child. An id
absent from the live board and every replica is still flagged, and the gate still refuses it.

Proof: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_board_replica_refs.py, 9 of 11 tests RED on db8b5c1168f, all
GREEN after; 0b1715a3f43's tests (test_kanban_false_signals.py) unchanged and green; 319 tests in 9
kanban files green; mutants M1-M8 on every new condition killed.
